10. **Revision:** Write three best practices for keeping API keys secure.

---

# 🎉 Python Fun Fact

Professional developers usually store API keys in environment variables or secret managers instead of placing them directly in source code.

---

# 🔄 Quick Recap

- API keys identify your application.
- Keys can be sent in headers or query parameters.
- Never share real API keys publicly.
- Secure key management is an important development skill.

